meta {
  name: 08_AuthorizationBoundaries
  seq: 8
}

docs {
  Scenario: What the endpoint policy accepts

    When no token is provided
    Then the request fails with 401
    When the token carries a scope the policy does not accept
    Then the request fails with 403
    When the token carries the portal enduser scope
    Then the request succeeds
    When the token carries the authorized parties scope
    Then the request succeeds

  Authorization negatives carry no problem body, so those steps assert the status alone.
}
